From: Li Guan <guanli.oerv@isrc.iscas.ac.cn>
Subject: [PATCH] Release extension resources when running on JUnit 5.12

JUnit 5.12 closes Store.CloseableResource entries when a test finishes.
Register the container and thread-local cleanup with that interface so
that the next test starts with its own base directory.

Upstream: downstream compatibility with JUnit 5.12
Reference: https://junit.org/junit5/docs/5.13.0/user-guide/#extensions-keeping-state
Signed-off-by: Li Guan <guanli.oerv@isrc.iscas.ac.cn>
---
diff --git a/src/main/java/org/codehaus/plexus/testing/PlexusExtension.java b/src/main/java/org/codehaus/plexus/testing/PlexusExtension.java
--- a/src/main/java/org/codehaus/plexus/testing/PlexusExtension.java
+++ b/src/main/java/org/codehaus/plexus/testing/PlexusExtension.java
@@ -64,7 +64,7 @@
  */
 public class PlexusExtension implements BeforeEachCallback, AfterEachCallback {
 
-    private static class PlexusClosableWrapper implements AutoCloseable {
+    private static class PlexusClosableWrapper implements ExtensionContext.Store.CloseableResource {
         private final PlexusContainer container;
 
         PlexusClosableWrapper(PlexusContainer container) {
@@ -108,7 +108,7 @@
         // must be done hear as this method is always executed
         extensionContextThreadLocal.set(context);
         context.getStore(PLEXUS_EXTENSION)
-                .put("threadLocalCloseable", (AutoCloseable) extensionContextThreadLocal::remove);
+                .put("threadLocalCloseable", (ExtensionContext.Store.CloseableResource) extensionContextThreadLocal::remove);
 
         // ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
         // Context Setup
